      "level": "warn",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 30 to 31; the oldest maintained major is 33 (the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  max-version 31 is below the oldest maintained major (33, the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), so the release covers only servers that no longer receive fixes.",
        "  min-version 30 reaches below the oldest maintained major (33), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "php-extensions",
      "lines": [
        "1 PHP extension is required by composer but not listed as <lib> in appinfo/info.xml:",
        "  iconv (phpoffice/phpspreadsheet)",
        "  A Nextcloud server need not load it. The server checks <lib> before it enables the app; composer only checks where it runs. Without the <lib> the app is enabled anyway and the first call into the extension fails at runtime."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "node-eol",
      "lines": [
        "engines.node ^20.0.0 in package.json admits only end-of-life Node lines: the release is built on Node 20, which reached end of life on 2026-04-30.",
        "  That Node receives no security fixes, and the lockfile is resolved for it. The oldest line still maintained is Node 22.",
        "  Node release dates from schedule.json of nodejs/Release, as of 2026-11-11."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0 (package.json), LICENSES/ holds AGPL-3.0-only.txt, AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt, Apache-2.0.txt, CC0-1.0.txt, MIT.txt.",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. An SPDX id there needs a <nextcloud> min-version of 31 or higher.",
        "  AGPL-3.0 (package.json) is a deprecated SPDX id, replaced because it does not say whether -only or -or-later is meant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as ^20.0.0 (package.json engines.node).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it.",
        "  The workflows read node-version from a variable, which is not resolved here, so whether CI builds on that major is not decidable from the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.json, superseded form), Stylelint (stylelint.config.cjs), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (tests/phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php), REUSE (REUSE.toml), EditorConfig (.editorconfig).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.json: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8."
      ]
    },
    {
